For the line $vb(u) times vb(r) = vb(u) times vb(a)$ against the plane $vb(n) dot vb(r) = vb(n) dot vb(b)$:

- If $vb(u) dot vb(n) != 0$, the intersection is the single point
$ vb(r) = ((vb(b) dot vb(n)) vb(u) - (vb(a) times vb(u)) times vb(n))/(vb(u) dot vb(n)). $

- If $vb(u) dot vb(n) = 0$, the direction is orthogonal to the normal, so the line either never meets the plane or lies entirely within it.
